# Pairs with NoResurrection. Reproduces #4362: the alias flips before T's
# shards are fenced, so a router whose cached pair names T keeps reading T
# after R has taken a write T never receives, and serves the older value.
MODULE: NoResurrectionFlipBeforeFence
TARGET: NoResurrection
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the alias flips before the old copy is fenced, so a stale router reads an older value from it
PERTURBS: ResizeFlip

--- FIND
ResizeFlip ==
    /\ rz = "copied"
    /\ fence = rzShards
--- REPLACE
ResizeFlip ==
    /\ rz = "copied"
\* MUTATION: the flip does not wait for the fence.
--- END